T* (- Harder to keep environments identical.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### 4.2 Option B: Dockerized services) Tj
T* (**Use when:** you need repeatable environments and cleaner delivery pipeline.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Pros:**) Tj
T* (- Consistent runtime from dev to production.) Tj
T* (- Easier CI/CD integration.) Tj
T* (- Better portability and rollback.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Cons:**) Tj
T* (- Additional container learning curve.) Tj
T* (- .NET Framework apps may require Windows containers and more setup care.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### 4.3 Option C: Kubernetes orchestration) Tj
T* (**Use when:** high-scale, multi-service, production-grade operations are required.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Pros:**) Tj
T* (- Auto-scaling, self-healing, rolling deployments.) Tj
T* (- Strong service management for larger SOC systems.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Cons:**) Tj
T* (- Highest operational complexity.) Tj
T* (- Overkill for small/medium coursework projects.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### 4.4 Recommended approach for this project) Tj
T* (- **Primary recommendation \(assignment fit\):** IIS + SQL Server for baseline demonstration.) Tj
T* (- **Forward-looking recommendation:** add Docker-based packaging for reproducibility and future scalability.) Tj
T* (- Document release steps, configuration strategy, backup policy, and rollback plan.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (---) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 5\) Conclusion / Evaluation Summary) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- The Cozy Comfort solution aligns with SOC intent by separating API services and client consumption.) Tj
T* (- To score higher, focus on:) Tj
T* (  1. Strong test evidence \(automated + manual traceability\).) Tj
T* (  2. Clear deployment justification with trade-off analysis.) Tj
T* (  3. Professional diagrams + maintainability rationale.) Tj
